   "shape_h": "p",
   "shape_m": "p",
   "html_text": "The twin foundations of Aristotle’s logic are the law of non-contradiction (LNC) (also known as the law of contradiction, LC) and the law of excluded middle (LEM). In Metaphysics Book ⟦M⟧ , LNC—“the firmest of all principles”—is defined as follows:",
